The function takes rows and returns only the PUBLIC_COLUMNS fields for each. The trailing comment lists the full table columns, which include private objector details, so the docstring should note that those are excluded. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add a docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and the public-only column filtering.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -3,6 +3,15 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return publicly exportable fields for each comment row.\n+\n+    Each row is a mapping containing at least the PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys.\n+    Only those columns are copied into the result, so private fields such as\n+    objector_name, objector_email, objector_phone and internal_note are never\n+    included in the output.\n+\n+    Returns a list of dicts, one per input row, in the same order.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
